==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|makes amends|making amends|made amends}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[repair]] a [[relationship]]; to [[make up]]; to [[resolve]] an [[argument]] or [[fight]]; to make [[reparations]] or [[redress]].
#: ''I hope they can stop fighting and '''make amends'''.''
#* {{quote-journal
|date=January 25, 2011
|author=Les Roopanarine
|title=Wigan 1 - 2 Aston Villa
|work=BBC
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9369947.stm
|page=
|passage=But with the home side likewise unable to make the most of a period of first-half ascendancy, Villa were swift to '''make amends''' on the restart.}}

